#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:38
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:40
msgid "`errorEx([name], [properties])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:41
msgid "Creates a new ErrorEx error type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:43
msgid ""
"`name`: the name of the new type (appears in the error message upon "
"throw; defaults to `Error.name`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:45
msgid ""
"`properties`: if supplied, used as a key/value dictionary of properties "
"to use when building up the stack message. Keys are property names that "
"are looked up on the error message, and then passed to function values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:48
msgid ""
"`line`: if specified and is a function, return value is added as a stack "
"entry (error-ex will indent for you). Passed the property value given the"
" key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:51
msgid ""
"`stack`: if specified and is a function, passed the value of the property"
" using the key, and the raw stack lines as a second argument. Takes no "
"return value (but the stack can be modified directly)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:54
msgid ""
"`message`: if specified and is a function, return value is used as new "
"`.message` value upon get. Passed the property value of the property "
"named by key, and the existing message is passed as the second argument "
"as an array of lines (suitable for multi-line messages)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:59
msgid ""
"Returns a constructor (Function) that can be used just like the regular "
"Error constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:93
msgid "`errorEx.line(str)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:94
msgid "Creates a stack line using a delimiter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:96 ../../source/error-ex_README.md:121
msgid ""
"This is a helper function. It is to be used in lieu of writing a value "
"object for `properties` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/error-ex_README.md:99
msgid "`str`: The string to create"
msgstr ""

